Critical
- The project does not compile:
- Product, inventory, and order repositories are undefined.
- createOrdersTable and createOrderItemsTable are undefined.
- cmd/sports-store/main.go:3 does nothing, so the application never starts.
- cmd/cli/cli.go:3 does nothing.
- internal/router/router.go:20 registers no routes.
High
- internal/database/repositories/payment_repository.go:34 has invalid SQL: RETURNING updated_at created_at needs a comma.
- Payment queries omit order_id from paymentColumns, so loaded payments lose their order ID.
- domains.Payment uses string timestamps while the database uses TIMESTAMPTZ; use time.Time.
- Coupon usage does not check is_active, starts_at, or expires_at.
- usage_limit_per_user is declared but cannot be enforced because coupon usage has no user ID or usage-tracking table.
- Repository methods for addresses, notifications, payments, and reviews operate by object ID alone. If handlers expose these directly, users could access or modify other users’ records.
Medium
- Sessions are stored as plaintext tokens. Hash session IDs before storing them.
- Redis credentials and TLS are hardcoded/insecure in internal/cache/cache.go:18-23.
- Category parent_id permits self-references and cycles.
- Default-address updates are not transactional and can fail when another address is already default.
- Cart, favorite, and notification list methods return “not found” for normal empty lists.
- Review likes/dislikes can be directly manipulated and have no per-user voting protection.
- Inventory/order ID types are inconsistent.